# Stage0 digests, COMMITTED deliberately — see docs/release/bootstrap.md §1.
# Pinned stage0 version: 0.1.10. Changing stage0 means changing this file,
# which means a reviewable commit rather than a server-side change.
#
# Moved 0.1.5 -> 0.1.9 in #2495, closing every difference recorded as owed
# against the 0.1.5 oracle in one move — 0.1.6/0.1.7/0.1.8 were released but
# this file was never repinned to any of them, so the debt had accumulated
# across three releases:
#
#   - #2084 (8c95c870) made lowering emit a terminator for a `@naked` body
#     that falls off the end. 0.1.5 emits none, so its block has no
#     terminator, DCE empties it and `computeReachable` reads `instrs[-1]` —
#     the 0.1.5 oracle SEGFAULTS on tests/cases/check_naked_body.bit under
#     `--dump-ir`. Against 0.1.5 both IR differentials diverged on exactly
#     three files — check_naked_body, check_naked_method, check_naked_params
#     — by one added `ret` each, and on nothing else in 627. This was
#     recorded here as owed against 0.1.6, which never got cut as a pin.
#   - #2040 (a7db72b3) seeds a bare arrow's expected type from a generic
#     callee — `mapped([1, 2, 3], x => x * 2)` typechecked and then refused
#     to lower. 0.1.5 infers `<invalid>`/`<error>` where this tree infers the
#     real type, diverging on run_generic_arrow.bit.
#   - #2275/#2277 (3b9654cb) types an unannotated arrow parameter from its
#     expected function type instead of leaving it at type 0 — silent
#     wrong-answer through `lowerIndex`'s Slice/Map/string fallthrough on one
#     face (#2275) and a spanless refusal to lower on the other (#2277).
#     Diverges from 0.1.5 on arrow_bare_param_index.bit and neighbouring
#     cases.
#
# None of the three is a regression, so softening a gate to absorb any of
# them would have written down a known difference instead of fixing it —
# exactly what #1883 deleted the expected-mismatch lists to prevent.
# Diagnosed on #2395; #2490 was closed as its duplicate.
#
# 0.1.9 was built by 0.1.8 in the normal way, and this repin's own
# `rm -rf bit-out && ./make` bootstrapped cleanly from stage0=0.1.9 in a single
# pass. The #1857 two-pass bootstrap via `BIT_STAGE0_BIN` was NOT needed and
# stays unused: nothing here depended on a fix that existed only downstream of
# the pinned compiler.
#
# Verified at release-cut time, on aarch64-macOS (#2495):
#   - all three artifacts downloaded ANONYMOUSLY (no token) and matched these
#     digests. An authenticated fetch proves nothing: a draft release answers a
#     token-bearing request and 404s an anonymous one.
#   - each artifact was smoke-tested UNPACKED by compiling and running a program
#     on hardware matching its triple, and asked for its own `--version`.
#   - x86_64-linux smoke-tested on REAL hardware, not emulation
#   - the shipped runtime was probed directly rather than inferred: #2014's OOB
#     panic fires (exit 2, `panic: index out of range`) and #2138's `parseFloat`
#     returns a quiet NaN, so `lib/libbitrt.a` in the shipped archive is this
#     tree's runtime, not a stale one (#2213's trap is absent).
#   - tag v0.1.9 lands on dab0b1fd, the commit that was tested (#1856: `gh
#     release create` tags the REMOTE head, so main is pushed BEFORE the
#     release is cut)
#
# RE-CONFIRMED independently when the pin moved (this commit): all three
# artifacts downloaded anonymously again, fresh, and their `shasum -a 256`
# matched the digests below before they were written here — not copied from
# the ticket that requested the move.
#
# REPRODUCIBILITY: 0.1.9 is the first PIN this file has ever named that was cut
# entirely after #2060's fix (d2f7105) landed — 0.1.6/0.1.7/0.1.8 all postdate
# it too, but none of them was ever pinned here, so 0.1.5 (which predates the
