#
# Moved 0.1.9 -> 0.1.10 in #2507, closing #2504. #2152 (fs.walk stops
# following symlinks) declares `extern function bit_rt_fs_is_symlink_w` in
# stdlib/fs/fs.bit:125, and `tools/build/artifacts.bit` imports `walk` from
# `std/fs` — Bit checks every extern in an imported module whether it is
# called or not. v0.1.9 was tagged at dab0b1fd, a DESCENDANT of 49e74817
# (the revert of #2152), nine minutes after 98787d48 had briefly added the
# symbol; #2152 was never re-landed to main before 0.1.9 was cut, so the
# released 0.1.9 archive's libbitrt.a never carried it. No repin to an
# EXISTING release (0.1.6-0.1.9) could have closed this — none of them was
# ever cut from a tree containing the symbol — it needed a release cut AFTER
# the fix landed again.
#
# THIS MOVE IS A DIFFERENT SHAPE FROM EVERY PRIOR ONE ON THIS FILE. Every
# earlier repin (0.1.5 -> 0.1.9 above, and 0.1.5's own predecessors) moved
# because the tree had OUTPACED the oracle on type inference or lowering —
# the old stage0 still built the driver end to end; it only diverged on
# typechecking or codegen for specific programs. This one moves because
# `tools/build` itself could not be built by the old stage0 AT ALL: the
# 0.1.9 archive was simply missing a runtime SYMBOL an extern declaration
# required, so `rm -rf bit-out && ./make` failed outright with
# `error[E0078]: 'extern function' bit_rt_fs_is_symlink_w is defined neither
# in the runtime archive nor by libSystem` on every fresh clone, not on some
# particular input program. The next person hitting a fresh E0078 on a
# newly-added extern should look here first — and note that a repin only
# closes it if the NEW release actually contains the symbol, which is why
# this entry proves that directly (see "Verified at repin time" below)
# rather than assuming it from the release notes.
#
# #2152 landed to main a second time at cf890e74, using the recipe #2504
# proved: ONE `./make` invocation with `BIT_LIBBITRT` pointed at a bootstrap
# `libbitrt.a` that the PINNED 0.1.9 stage0 itself compiled from the working
# tree's `runtime/` sources (via scripts/g2archive.sh) — `runtime/` does not
# import `std/fs`, it only DEFINES the symbol, so 0.1.9 could build a fresh
# archive containing it even though its own bundled archive lacked it.
# `BIT_STAGE0_BIN` (the #1857 two-pass hatch) was NOT needed for this cut;
# the narrower `BIT_LIBBITRT` sufficed in a single pass. 0.1.10 was then
# released directly from cf890e74 — the SAME commit main is at when this
# entry was written — so there is no tag-off-mainline provenance oddity to
# record here.
#
